I’ll first inspect the pattern, metadata, and the provided diffraction workflow, then build a falsifiable candidate ledger before refining any final phase set. I’ll keep candidate comparisons on a common GSAS-II project/settings and verify the exported CIFs and replayed profile at the end.

The chemistry points to Ca–W–O with possible carbonate/oxide carryover at 650 °C, while the high low-angle background suggests the raw scan may include a substantial decaying background. I’m now extracting peak families and auditing the local COD/DARA and GSAS-II interfaces so the candidate inventory is based on all same-composition entries plus plausible Ca–W–O/oxide prototypes.

